# Run files are derived data: `npm run eval` regenerates them in ~3 s from
# inputs pinned by SHA-256, which is what Phase 1 bought. The *.run.json
# sidecars beside them ARE committed — they hold the provenance, which is the
# part that does not regenerate. Per-file rather than ignoring results/, so 2.4
# can commit metric-validation.txt from the same tree. See EVALUATION.md §8.5.
results/runs/*.run
results/runs/*.zero.txt
# 2.7's sweep, and the one place §8.5's rule had to be EXTENDED rather than
# applied. Sidecars are committed above because per-run provenance does not
# regenerate. At grid scale it does: the grid is committed code
# (backend/scripts/sweep-v1.js), and all 342 points share one set of
# SHA-256-pinned inputs, one environment and one git commit. So the committed
# unit moves up a level — results/sweeps/v1-sweep.manifest.json carries what
# every point's sidecar would have carried in common plus the per-point digest
# table, and v1-threshold.csv carries the results. A NAMED configuration still
# gets a sidecar in results/runs/; a GRID POINT gets a CSV row. §8.5.
results/sweeps/runs/
# The 2.4 validation venv. The pins that matter are committed in
# scripts/requirements.txt, hashed; the installed tree is derived from them.
scripts/.venv/
